<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n102896" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εος</span>, τό, 
			Ep.
		 dat. pl. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.71
				</span></i>
			, al., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τεκέεσσι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					3.160
				</span></i>
			, al.:—poet. for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τέκνον</span>, <i><span class="en">
				18.63
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				24.36
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				216
			</span></i>, al.; as a term of endearment from elders to their youngers, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φίλον τέκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.437
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				444
			</span></i>, etc.: also in <i><span class="en">
				Alc.
				<u>Supp.</u>
				10.7
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>I.</u>
				6(5).30
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				B.
				6.13
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Th.</u>
				203
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				677
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>HF</u>
				439
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Hec.</u>
				475
			</span></i> (mostly lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> of animals, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				8.248
			</span></i>: esp. in pl. <i>the young</i>, <i><span class="en">
				12.222
			</span></i>, al., <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Pl.</u>
				292
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b> metaph., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δυσσεβίας μὲν ὕβρις τέκος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					534
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.).</div>
